1
00:00:00,062 --> 00:00:05,312
(Mrs Cooper:)For example, if Shelly was aboard,
he'd write "smart mouth" on his pigeon.

2
00:00:05,484 --> 00:00:08,194
And then: Bam!

3
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:11,444
(Sheldon:)The Lord giveth
and the Lord bloweth away.

4
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:15,790
(Sheldon:)Well, Mom, according to my itinerary
for our weekend together...

5
00:00:15,952 --> 00:00:18,912
(Sheldon:)- ...the fun begins with fried chicken.
- Sounds delicious.

6
00:00:19,081 --> 00:00:21,711
Good, because I got you everything
you need to make it.

7
00:00:21,917 --> 00:00:23,497
(Sheldon:)You are in for a treat.

8
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:26,340
(Sheldon:)My mother's fried chicken
is why we had to buy my dad...

9
00:00:26,505 --> 00:00:28,755
(Sheldon:)...the extra large coffin.

10
00:00:29,466 --> 00:00:32,176
(Leonard:)Sheldon, she just got off the plane.
She doesn't wanna cook.

11
00:00:32,344 --> 00:00:33,594
(Sheldon:)Of course she does.

12
00:00:33,762 --> 00:00:36,352
(Sheldon:)Making me food is her way of saying
"l love you."

13
00:00:36,515 --> 00:00:38,145
Making me food when too tired...

14
00:00:38,308 --> 00:00:40,688
(Sheldon:)...is her way of saying
"l really love you."

15
00:00:40,852 --> 00:00:43,272
(Mrs Cooper:)I wouldn't mind going out
for a bite, Sheldon.

16
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:46,650
(Sheldon:)Won't that spoil our appetites
for the chicken you're gonna make?

17
00:00:46,817 --> 00:00:48,567
(Leonard:)All right.
We're going out. You like sushi?

18
00:00:48,735 --> 00:00:50,275
There's a great place down the street.

19
00:00:50,445 --> 00:00:54,995
(Mrs Cooper:)I've never had it, but there's no harm
in trying something new.

20
00:00:55,158 --> 00:00:57,538
(Sheldon:)There's a lot of harm
in trying something new.

21
00:00:57,744 --> 00:01:00,704
(Sheldon:)That's why we test out drugs
and cosmetics on bunny rabbits.

22
00:01:01,957 --> 00:01:04,127
(Leonard:)Sheldon, you're talking
Iike a crazy person.

23
00:01:04,292 --> 00:01:07,842
(Mrs Cooper:)Actually, I had him tested as a child.

24
00:01:08,004 --> 00:01:09,134
(Mrs Cooper:)Doctor says he's fine.

25
00:01:10,132 --> 00:01:12,552
- Told you.
- I do regret not following up...

26
00:01:12,717 --> 00:01:18,027
(Mrs Cooper:)...with that specialist in Houston.

